  "answer": "Other users have already requested this feature, which is a schedule for Awake with a start time, an end time and days of the week. PowerToys#27790 is the main request. It was marked as tracked under PowerToys#24846, so add your +1 or use case there. The archive doesn't show that it has been implemented. Awake can't schedule by time and day yet. As a workaround, use the Awake CLI with an expiry time. For example, a Windows Task Scheduler task can run `PowerToys.Awake.exe --expire-at=18:00:00` on weekdays at 09:00. Another option is a task that triggers when the PC resumes from sleep and restarts Awake with the expiry time. PowerToys#27790 has an example PowerShell script for this."
